# ============================================================================
# What must NOT be uploaded to Vercel.
# ============================================================================
#
# MEASURED, not assumed: the first deploy uploaded 2,526 files because the Vercel
# CLI ships the WORKING DIRECTORY, not the git tree — so gitignored files go up
# too. Verified publicly reachable on the live deployment before this file existed:
#
#   /.backup/index.html.1905              the previous build, served to anyone
#   /dev-server.js                        server source
#   /.workbuddy-ai/memory/MEMORY.md       internal project notes
#   /db/migrations/*.sql                  the database schema
#
# `.env` and `.env.local` returned 404 — Vercel blocks those itself. Everything
# else needed this list.
#
# If you add a top-level directory, ask whether it should be public. The default
# for a static deploy is YES, which is the wrong default for all of these.
# ============================================================================

# the previous build, kept for reference — never served
.backup/

# local scratch: headless-browser profiles, audit scripts, screenshots, logs
.freebuff/

# AI session memory: internal notes, decisions, risk register
.workbuddy-ai/

# the database schema and the migration runner
db/

# product and architecture docs — internal
docs/

# the local dev server (it runs the api/* handlers with a service-role key)
dev-server.js

# version control and the Vercel link itself
.git/
.vercel/

# secrets — Vercel blocks these, but they should never be in the upload either
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# repo furniture that has no business being served
.gitignore
README.md
LICENSE
package.json
package-lock.json
